bloom-core (verdantbloom.bar landing page)

This module contains a port of "newcal" - The New Calendar - Kotlin implementation.

  Source:   newcal, kotlin/src/main/kotlin/com/ralphlandon/newcal/NewCal.kt
            and kotlin/src/test/kotlin/com/ralphlandon/newcal/NewCalTest.kt
  Author:   Copyright (c) ralph7c2
  License:  MIT (the upstream README states "License: MIT"; upstream ships no separate LICENSE file,
            so the standard MIT text is reproduced below)

Ported files:
  src/commonMain/kotlin/bar/verdantbloom/bloom/core/NewCal.kt
  src/commonTest/kotlin/bar/verdantbloom/bloom/core/NewCalTest.kt

Changes made in the port:
  - package and API shape: implements bar.verdantbloom.bloom.api.NewCalendar and returns NewCalDate
    (which carries dayOfWeek and modifier as fields) instead of the upstream Date class;
  - day counting uses floor division, so instants before 1970 that are not on a day boundary map to
    the correct day (upstream truncates towards zero);
  - the year roll-over loop compares against the real year length; upstream used "days > 365" and
    indexed past the season list on 21 December of every non-leap New Calendar year;
  - added formatTime (HH:MM:SS UTC);
  - tests: java.time replaced by a pure Kotlin civil-date helper so they run on Kotlin/JS; the two
    upstream cases written with day 0 for the leap day use LEAP_DAY (-1); extra cases added.

